cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use or build on this dossier, please cite it as below. Primary sources are cited inside each file."
title: "Dog ageing × AI: a research dossier on AlphaFold, IBM MAMMAL, canine foundation models, and why dogs age fast"
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: "Ebin Babu"
    family-names: "Thomas"
    alias: "ebt55"
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ebt55/dog-ageing-ai-dossier"
date-released: "2026-10-04"
license: CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - dog ageing
  - canine longevity
  - AlphaFold
  - MAMMAL
  - foundation models
  - geroscience
  - wolves
  - IGF-1
abstract: >-
  A source-cited, cross-model-verified research dossier covering AlphaFold
  (history, how it works, how to use it, dog/wolf coverage), IBM's MAMMAL
  biomedical foundation model (paper deep dive and a fact-check of a popular
  video about it), the landscape of AI models and organisations relevant to
  dogs and wolves, the biology of why dogs age faster than humans (and why
  large breeds age fastest), longevity interventions and gene editing in dogs,
  and a ranked set of research paths for understanding and changing dog ageing.
  Produced with AI research agents (Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Fable 5.1) and
  audited claim-by-claim by a second model family; not peer-reviewed.
